{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Let the waters be gathered.</b> Since the deep (תהום), which is water and earth in the likeness of murky water, existed, the sacred utterance needed to decree that the waters beneath the heavens, which were on high, be gathered to one low place below, and that the earth rise upward until the dry land appear and become fit for settlement. Now these are two decrees contrary to their natures, for the nature of earth is to descend below and the nature of waters is to rise above; and now He decreed upon the waters, which had filled the entire world, that they descend below like the nature of earth, in the manner of what is written (Job 38:30) ״כאבן מים יתחבאו״, and He decreed upon the earth that it rise above like the nature of waters, and this is what is written (Psalms 136:6) ״לרוקע הארץ על המים כי לעולם חסדו״, for this is everlasting kindness for the perpetuation of civilization and the creatures within it. And this is what is written (Psalms 36:7) ״צדקתך כהררי אל משפטיך תהום רבה״, for thereby the righteousness of the Holy One, blessed be He, was revealed when He set His judgments in the great deep, in order that the waters descend contrary to their nature, so as to deliver man and beast, that is, the living creatures of the earth. And there is further to explain ״ותראה היבשה״ — 'and the dry land appeared' — that dryness should be visible in it, for this is why it is called יבשה (dry land): as long as it is moist it cannot bring forth fruits; and now, when the dryness was seen in it, the work of the waters was completed, and concerning it He declared ״כי טוב״." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> ״יקוו המים״ — He made a measure for the waters, as it says (Zechariah 1:16) ״וקו ינטה על ירושלים״, and as it says (Job 28:25) ״ומים תכן במדה״. He apportioned half in the firmament and half in the ocean, as it is written (Psalms 65:6) ״פלג אלהים מלא מים״." "Another interpretation: <b>Let the waters be gathered</b> — let the waters be gathered for Me for what I am destined to do with them and to flood the entire world in the Flood. A parable: to a king who built a palace and settled in it mute tenants. They arose and greeted the king. The king said: If, when I settled mute tenants in it, they thus concur and greet me by gesture and with a finger, then if I were to settle in it intelligent tenants, how much the more so! He arose and settled intelligent tenants in it. They arose and seized the palace, saying: The palace of the king is none other than ours! The king said: Let the palace return to what it was. So too, at the beginning of the world's creation, the praise of the Holy One, blessed be He, ascended from the waters, as it says (Psalms 93:4) ״מקולות מים רבים״. The generation of Enosh arose and rebelled against Him, and the generation of the Flood arose and rebelled against Him. The Holy One, blessed be He, said: Let these depart, and let the waters stand in their place, as it is written (Genesis 7) ״ויהי הגשם על הארץ״." "<b>To one place.</b> The entire world was entirely water within water, and you say ״to one place״? Rather, the lesser held the greater. End."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:24:39.739818293Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}